1
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,678
Main gate is clear.
No movement of civilians or vehicles.

2
00:00:13,263 --> 00:00:14,514
Clear.

3
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,564
Entry complete.

4
00:00:23,565 --> 00:00:24,566
Copy.

5
00:00:32,324 --> 00:00:34,325
Moving to the basement
in 30 seconds.

6
00:00:34,326 --> 00:00:36,035
Five-minute-interval check-in.

7
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,037
Roger.

8
00:01:13,282 --> 00:01:15,867
Marco, M, secure the basement server
on level one.

9
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:20,037
The rest you, follow me to the mall.

10
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:21,415
Yes, chief!

11
00:01:27,004 --> 00:01:30,047
Pasin, what happened
to my uncle and Minhye?

12
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,508
Pasin…

13
00:01:32,134 --> 00:01:33,719
don't do this.

14
00:01:35,137 --> 00:01:36,430
Stay still.

15
00:01:37,681 --> 00:01:38,849
It's all over.

16
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:57,159
I got Jian now.

17
00:01:58,201 --> 00:01:59,369
Let Atti go.

18
00:02:01,997 --> 00:02:04,958
Pasin, it's me.

19
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:07,878
Hold for a second.

20
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:11,464
-  Dad.
- Atti?

21
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:13,215
Are you all right?

22
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:14,592
Are you hurt anywhere?

23
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:15,677
I'm fine.

24
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:18,805
I'm okay. Really okay.

25
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:23,060
Atti? Everything is going
to be okay now, Atti!

26
00:02:23,769 --> 00:02:24,770
Atti.

27
00:02:30,025 --> 00:02:31,652
You saved my son.

28
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:36,031
- Thank you, Jinman.
-  No, don't thank me.

29
00:02:38,492 --> 00:02:41,578
Starting from now on,
I'm your son's kidnapper.

30
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:44,414
Listen carefully.

31
00:02:45,499 --> 00:02:47,751
Stop being Babylon's little puppet.

32
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:52,631
Protect your son by protecting Jian.

33
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:56,218
Make sure that Jian doesn't die!

34
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:04,226
Remember, Pasin,
your son's life is on the line.

35
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:29,835
What about my uncle?

36
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:32,003
Jinman is all right, Jian.

37
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:41,346
I am… sorry about everything.

38
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:44,099
I'll explain all of it later.

39
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:46,351
We have to leave.

40
00:03:48,061 --> 00:03:49,062
Hurry, Jian.

41
00:04:00,532 --> 00:04:02,200
Okay, keep going.

42
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:19,634
-  Get her alive!
-  Brother!

43
00:04:29,478 --> 00:04:30,479
Go!

44
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:47,204
Go!

45
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:52,542
Go!

46
00:05:28,119 --> 00:05:29,120
The gun at the end.

47
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:42,050
Hold tight.

48
00:05:46,471 --> 00:05:47,597
Be careful.

49
00:05:57,107 --> 00:05:58,859
Go, little slug.

50
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,485
Master.

51
00:06:19,379 --> 00:06:21,464
Master!

52
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:24,384
That door…

53
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:29,472
it can't be opened from here.

54
00:06:35,729 --> 00:06:36,897
Listen up, Jeong Jian.

55
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:40,692
There could be a situation
where you lose an arm.

56
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:45,071
What happens then?
Don't try to recover the arm you lost.

57
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:48,491
You should protect the one you still have.

58
00:06:57,584 --> 00:06:58,793
We have to go.

59
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:28,364
- Where is Jeong Jian?
-  In there.

60
00:07:28,365 --> 00:07:30,325
Pull the handle on the last rifle.

61
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:32,952
- I'm going after her.
- Yes, chief!

62
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:14,012
Shit.

63
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,604
We're almost there.
You have to get up, okay?

64
00:09:23,605 --> 00:09:24,689
We're almost there.

65
00:09:41,206 --> 00:09:42,456
Brother.

66
00:09:42,457 --> 00:09:43,458
Brother.

67
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:46,669
You… you go first.

68
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:49,671
- Better hurry up, Jian.
- That's not allowed.

69
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:51,091
Stand up. Give me your arm.

70
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:55,804
I need just a minute to rest.

71
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:04,687
We're almost there.

72
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:08,273
Brother, get up.

73
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:09,609
We're going together.

74
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:18,700
What?

75
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:20,994
Hey, stupid shit.
This isn't funny.

76
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:22,789
Open the door. Open it!

77
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:25,458
Brother, open the door!

78
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:28,502
-  Jeong Jian.
-  Open the door!

79
00:10:28,503 --> 00:10:32,799
- Thank you for everything. Go live.
-  Open the door!

80
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:38,930
Brother, please open the door! Open it!

81
00:10:39,556 --> 00:10:41,807
- Hyung…
-  Brother, open the door!

82
00:10:41,808 --> 00:10:44,561
see you in a few minutes.

83
00:11:14,174 --> 00:11:15,216
Stop it.

84
00:11:27,896 --> 00:11:29,063
Stop it.

85
00:11:31,149 --> 00:11:32,817
Don't do it.

86
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:06,893
Son of a bitch!

87
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:24,911
Breaching.

88
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:27,997
Move into the underground passage.

89
00:12:28,665 --> 00:12:29,916
Right now!

90
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:39,299
Oh, right in front of it,
there's a small room,

91
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,510
like the old shopping mall.

92
00:12:41,511 --> 00:12:44,639
From there, you can just…

93
00:12:45,056 --> 00:12:48,642
- …burn the whole shopping mall down.
-  Why?

94
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:49,893
Why?

95
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:53,105
Your escaping through
means that's an emergency situation

96
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:55,316
and you can't leave any traces behind.

97
00:14:15,772 --> 00:14:16,981
Retreat!

98
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:07,049
Wow, you killed everyone.

99
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:22,440
Jian, do you get it now?

100
00:16:23,316 --> 00:16:25,526
The kind of hell you'll have to live with.

101
00:16:46,756 --> 00:16:53,763
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

102
00:16:57,767 --> 00:17:00,686
EPISODE 07
THE ENEMY OF MY ENEMY

103
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:19,324
So, what do I get out of this?

104
00:19:19,325 --> 00:19:22,285
If you manage to persuade
the Code Reds for us,

105
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:24,120
we'll provide free weapons.

106
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:27,707
For every operation completed,
there's a separate profit-sharing rate.

107
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:28,709
Guaranteed.

108
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,172
That's very generous.

109
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:37,093
But as you've probably heard,

110
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:41,179
I've been retired
from this business for a long time.

111
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:45,434
What exactly do you get out of being so
generous to a washed-up guy like me? Hm?

112
00:19:45,810 --> 00:19:49,187
It seems all the Code Reds
take orders from you.

113
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:50,189
That's why we're here.

114
00:19:51,065 --> 00:19:53,024
When you make a move, they all follow.

115
00:19:53,025 --> 00:19:58,238
That entire network also happens
to include the client list that we want.

116
00:19:58,239 --> 00:20:00,990
I get that.
But that's fallen apart by now.

117
00:20:00,991 --> 00:20:02,535
Just us small fries left.

118
00:20:03,119 --> 00:20:05,621
Well, that happens
to be what big corporations fear.

119
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,707
Start-ups and the relentless small fries.

120
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:12,712
For instance, Jeong Jinman's murthehelp.
It's a good business model.

121
00:20:13,379 --> 00:20:15,047
Speaking of Jinman…

122
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:25,599
If you're able to capture Jeong Jinman
or Jeong Jian,

123
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:29,854
Babylon will kindly offer you
this token of goodwill.

124
00:21:57,149 --> 00:22:01,904
From now on,
all the Code Greens are under protection.

125
00:22:04,198 --> 00:22:05,199
So, um…

126
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:09,995
…are you Kusanagi or Jin? I'm confused.

127
00:22:10,621 --> 00:22:12,540
Are you Korean or Japanese?

128
00:22:13,791 --> 00:22:15,292
You're taking the money back?

129
00:22:16,377 --> 00:22:18,212
Fine. Okay.

130
00:22:19,547 --> 00:22:23,675
I'm Korean. I've just been working
in Japan for so long--

131
00:22:23,676 --> 00:22:28,264
So you're saying you're a Korean woman
using a Japanese surname?

132
00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:30,307
Ms. Yoon Sujin?

133
00:22:33,936 --> 00:22:37,231
One's nationality doesn't really matter,
does it?

134
00:22:37,898 --> 00:22:40,191
- We work on a global scale.
-  Of course, it does.

135
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:41,986
It's not as simple as you think.

136
00:22:43,237 --> 00:22:46,447
I'm the 37th generation
of the Ahns of Sunheung

137
00:22:46,448 --> 00:22:48,199
and the eldest grandson.

138
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:52,787
My direct ancestors include Ahn Junggeun
and Ahn Changho.

139
00:22:52,788 --> 00:22:54,999
What do you mean? For real?

140
00:22:56,834 --> 00:22:58,459
Ah. Sorry.

141
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:00,587
I'd never take
a Japanese name.

142
00:23:00,588 --> 00:23:04,340
My ancestors died protecting our country
from all those bastards.

143
00:23:04,341 --> 00:23:06,719
We should all be working together.

144
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:09,762
Business is business.

145
00:23:09,763 --> 00:23:14,393
It shouldn't matter
whether we're Korean or Japanese.

146
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,775
It's not like you're here
fighting for Korean independence.

147
00:23:24,278 --> 00:23:28,198
Yeah, who am I? I'm not some guy
trying to save my country.

148
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:30,784
The truth is…

149
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:33,412
I don't like you.

150
00:23:34,163 --> 00:23:36,874
You're a suit who looks like
you've never gotten blood on your hands.

151
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:42,337
You believe that your money can buy
you anything and keep your hands clean.

152
00:23:42,338 --> 00:23:44,548
Yeah? You're disgusting.

153
00:23:45,716 --> 00:23:48,468
You sit behind a desk
while your subordinates do everything.

154
00:23:48,469 --> 00:23:49,678
Jeez.

155
00:23:51,055 --> 00:23:54,307
The Chosenjins have such a narrow view.
The view…

156
00:23:54,308 --> 00:23:55,351
What's that?

157
00:23:58,395 --> 00:23:59,605
Hey, you listen to me.

158
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:04,025
If you want to keep eating
that meat you like so much,

159
00:24:04,026 --> 00:24:05,778
you should be careful about what you say.

160
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:10,240
I could obliterate…

161
00:24:12,117 --> 00:24:14,327
this whole place right now.

162
00:24:23,587 --> 00:24:24,713
Hm.

163
00:24:25,255 --> 00:24:26,632
It's okay.

164
00:24:27,967 --> 00:24:30,511
On something so trivial.

165
00:24:49,405 --> 00:24:52,992
This meat's texture
is worth the price.

166
00:25:00,666 --> 00:25:03,210
Ahn Seongbeom, I understand your position.

167
00:25:04,253 --> 00:25:06,422
It's always the cowards
who show their teeth first.

168
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:24,857
Babylon doesn't put people
behind a desk…

169
00:25:26,859 --> 00:25:29,111
unless they've gotten blood
on their hands.

170
00:26:08,901 --> 00:26:10,444
Spread out and find them.

171
00:26:49,108 --> 00:26:50,692
Light in the face of death…

172
00:26:52,236 --> 00:26:53,695
Light in the face of death…

173
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:17,636
Q! Q!

174
00:27:18,428 --> 00:27:19,429
Are you okay?

175
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:23,267
This way.

176
00:28:12,608 --> 00:28:13,609
Give me your gun.

177
00:28:25,162 --> 00:28:26,163
There she is.

178
00:28:49,061 --> 00:28:50,854
"JW."

179
00:28:56,693 --> 00:28:58,319
BABYLON
JW

180
00:28:58,320 --> 00:29:00,113
JW UNION

181
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:06,286
YOUR FINAL JOURNEY. WE WILL
ACCOMPANY YOU PEACEFULLY AND SAFELY

182
00:29:12,250 --> 00:29:14,878
K, I have important information.

183
00:29:16,129 --> 00:29:18,839
Yes, understood.
The intelligence team will look into it.

184
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:20,591
I'll contact you with an update.

185
00:29:20,592 --> 00:29:24,804
She decided to act on her own
without reporting to me first.

186
00:29:24,805 --> 00:29:27,516
- Should I tell her to return to the base?
- No, it's all right.

187
00:29:28,725 --> 00:29:31,645
Q can be preoccupied
with catching Jeong Jian on her own.

188
00:29:33,981 --> 00:29:36,233
We'll focus on capturing Jeong Jinman.

189
00:29:58,088 --> 00:30:00,966
We're gonna check out the other server
on basement level one.

190
00:30:03,885 --> 00:30:07,389
I wouldn't have worn this
if I knew it'd be so filthy down here.

191
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:14,813
- Hey!
- Me? Yes?

192
00:30:22,946 --> 00:30:24,281
Oh, my God.

193
00:30:29,828 --> 00:30:30,829
Hold on.

194
00:30:32,039 --> 00:30:35,417
- Q survived all of this?
-  Yeah.

195
00:30:36,543 --> 00:30:39,004
That bitch has nine lives.

196
00:31:04,905 --> 00:31:06,531
Hey, President Choi.
What happened?

197
00:31:14,581 --> 00:31:15,582
What?

198
00:31:38,688 --> 00:31:41,191
Oh, noona, you're awake.

199
00:31:44,778 --> 00:31:45,987
It's been a while.

200
00:31:48,281 --> 00:31:49,657
Don't you have school?

201
00:31:49,658 --> 00:31:50,992
We're on break.

202
00:31:57,165 --> 00:31:58,542
Where are we?

203
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:05,257
Gonna answer it?

204
00:32:07,634 --> 00:32:08,677
Should I?

205
00:32:37,539 --> 00:32:38,540
Hello.

206
00:32:39,457 --> 00:32:40,458
Jeong Jian.

207
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:42,752
Uncle.

208
00:33:03,190 --> 00:33:06,400
So even
after all that "sea of fire" bullshit,

209
00:33:06,401 --> 00:33:09,904
you're telling me we still need
Jeong Jinman and Jeong Jian?

210
00:33:09,905 --> 00:33:11,113
Yes.

211
00:33:11,114 --> 00:33:13,866
It's their biometric information
that opens the location data

212
00:33:13,867 --> 00:33:15,493
from murthehelp's codes.

213
00:33:17,287 --> 00:33:18,622
You.

214
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:29,757
Why are you bouncing around,
listening to music

215
00:33:29,758 --> 00:33:32,677
as if you're being paid
to half-ass your work?

216
00:33:33,553 --> 00:33:35,804
Do you think you're here
for college credit?

217
00:33:35,805 --> 00:33:40,143
You seem to be treating this like
some kind of part-time job or something.

218
00:33:41,436 --> 00:33:44,481
If you children don't extract
the data immediately,

219
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:48,235
you'll all disappear,
never to be found again.

220
00:33:50,070 --> 00:33:52,530
I'll put you all in a meat grinder.
Understood?

221
00:33:57,452 --> 00:33:59,329
- Is that clear?
-  Yes.

222
00:34:00,872 --> 00:34:01,873
Good.

223
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:06,086
Uh… Sorry.

224
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:08,879
-  Hm?
- I think… I think

225
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,382
we might need better equipment.

226
00:34:17,264 --> 00:34:19,182
Get whatever you need.

227
00:34:39,077 --> 00:34:42,413
So Minhye, she's as tough as they say.

228
00:34:42,414 --> 00:34:45,875
She crawled out of the water on her own,
even after she was shot.

229
00:34:52,674 --> 00:34:53,925
She's lucky.

230
00:34:54,843 --> 00:34:56,720
The bullet didn't hit any vital areas.

231
00:34:57,804 --> 00:35:00,223
I can't believe
Pasin would do that to her.

232
00:35:42,807 --> 00:35:47,103
You can think of this place
as Code Red's headquarters.

233
00:35:48,021 --> 00:35:51,357
Doesn't look like much,
but a tank couldn't get through this door.

234
00:35:51,358 --> 00:35:53,068
It's made with a special alloy.

235
00:36:06,790 --> 00:36:09,250
Most of these guns were purchased
from your uncle.

236
00:36:10,043 --> 00:36:14,463
When jobs come through murthehelp,
Code Reds would come to this place.

237
00:36:14,464 --> 00:36:15,924
It's more secure this way.

238
00:36:16,633 --> 00:36:20,053
Collecting their weapons here
prevents them from killing on impulse.

239
00:36:21,763 --> 00:36:23,556
Jeong Jinman came up with that.

240
00:36:24,766 --> 00:36:27,811
Hard to believe,
but I used to manage all of this.

241
00:36:29,020 --> 00:36:31,731
And thanks to someone, I guess I'm back.

242
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:36,194
My uncle mentioned this.

243
00:37:05,765 --> 00:37:08,476
Hey. Are you sure?

244
00:37:12,021 --> 00:37:13,314
Even if I'm not…

245
00:37:16,359 --> 00:37:17,944
I can't just sit and do nothing.

246
00:37:18,653 --> 00:37:19,696
Jian.

247
00:37:24,617 --> 00:37:25,744
It's good to go.

248
00:37:46,055 --> 00:37:49,725
We've seized and taken over
murthehelp's underground base.

249
00:37:49,726 --> 00:37:51,727
Most of their operatives
have been eliminated,

250
00:37:51,728 --> 00:37:53,521
and we possess their data.

251
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:55,773
It's currently being analyzed.

252
00:37:55,774 --> 00:37:58,526
Is there any risk
this could become a problem?

253
00:37:58,735 --> 00:38:00,069
Hm…

254
00:38:03,239 --> 00:38:04,698
Absolutely not.

255
00:38:04,699 --> 00:38:07,701
They are going to hook our server
into their supercomputer

256
00:38:07,702 --> 00:38:09,704
to try to siphon data from murthehelp.

257
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:13,832
This is a functioning server,
but in an emergency,

258
00:38:13,833 --> 00:38:15,418
it's also an electric bomb.

259
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:18,796
If an unauthorized user
tries to access it,

260
00:38:18,797 --> 00:38:23,133
it'll overheat, disabling power completely
within a one-kilometer radius.

261
00:38:23,134 --> 00:38:24,886
They'll reboot it, but it'll take time.

262
00:38:26,513 --> 00:38:28,430
It looks like
we'll have about five minutes

263
00:38:28,431 --> 00:38:30,600
on the server's emergency battery.

264
00:38:31,726 --> 00:38:36,063
But if the main base loses all power,
wouldn't it be impossible to hack?

265
00:38:36,064 --> 00:38:37,857
Maybe if you're trying to hack remotely.

266
00:38:38,900 --> 00:38:40,692
Brother predicted this exact situation.

267
00:38:40,693 --> 00:38:43,363
So we had the mole
plant satellite comms inside.

268
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:46,365
We can extract their data
at the same time.

269
00:38:46,366 --> 00:38:49,744
Very good work,
Branch Chief Kusanagi.

270
00:38:50,411 --> 00:38:54,874
As promised, I'm allowing you
to take managerial control of murthehelp.

271
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:59,879
I trust that you will be able to grow it
into Babylon's business partner.

272
00:39:00,630 --> 00:39:03,340
Yes. Thank you so much.

273
00:39:03,341 --> 00:39:04,550
The time is right.

274
00:39:04,551 --> 00:39:07,761
Make sure to rename murthehelp
to something more fitting.

275
00:39:07,762 --> 00:39:10,932
Of course, I'll take care of it.

276
00:39:11,516 --> 00:39:12,517
One more thing.

277
00:39:14,310 --> 00:39:16,980
How has Jeong Jinman been dealt with?

278
00:39:19,274 --> 00:39:22,527
Prepare for brother's parting gift,
you Babylon shitheads.

279
00:39:33,371 --> 00:39:35,331
Jeong Jinman is…

280
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:40,044
It worked.

281
00:39:43,089 --> 00:39:45,508
Tell them to get the backup power online.

282
00:39:46,467 --> 00:39:48,844
While they're all losing
their minds trying to restore power,

283
00:39:48,845 --> 00:39:52,348
all we have to do is connect our server
that we swapped with their server.

284
00:39:52,849 --> 00:39:55,560
- And that's it.
-  I get it.

285
00:39:56,060 --> 00:39:58,313
That's why there's a mole
in Babylon, right?

286
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:16,789
Connection to mole complete.

287
00:40:18,166 --> 00:40:19,959
It's my time to shine.

288
00:40:20,543 --> 00:40:22,544
- How long?
- One minute.

289
00:40:22,545 --> 00:40:24,046
Reset the main breaker?

290
00:40:24,047 --> 00:40:25,340
Hey, what's going on?

291
00:40:37,477 --> 00:40:39,520
The backup power is up and running.

292
00:40:47,528 --> 00:40:48,905
What's wrong with the server?

293
00:40:53,451 --> 00:40:55,202
I almost had a heart attack, man.

294
00:41:02,043 --> 00:41:03,711
What? Something's wrong.

295
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:06,297
What?

296
00:41:09,175 --> 00:41:11,551
Open your damn mouth. What is it?

297
00:41:11,552 --> 00:41:15,056
The inside of the server is, um,
completely empty.

298
00:41:22,730 --> 00:41:24,273
And now it's time to take a look.

299
00:41:24,983 --> 00:41:27,110
What has Babylon been up to for decades?

300
00:41:27,777 --> 00:41:28,987
Those assholes.

301
00:41:53,970 --> 00:41:56,472
Chief, is this the right place?

302
00:41:58,599 --> 00:41:59,600
Q?

303
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:13,406
Sorry.

304
00:42:14,615 --> 00:42:17,743
At least let's change our clothes.

305
00:42:17,744 --> 00:42:19,037
We stink.

306
00:42:21,497 --> 00:42:22,832
And we're starving.

307
00:42:33,634 --> 00:42:34,635
So?

308
00:42:39,015 --> 00:42:41,975
For now, I've notified the staff
that the outage was caused

309
00:42:41,976 --> 00:42:43,769
by a mechanical malfunction,

310
00:42:43,770 --> 00:42:47,440
and I've had employees sign non-disclosure
agreements to keep them all quiet.

311
00:42:48,733 --> 00:42:50,777
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

312
00:42:51,402 --> 00:42:53,529
Nothing's been reported in the news yet.

313
00:42:54,447 --> 00:42:56,783
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

314
00:43:00,161 --> 00:43:01,788
Can I say something?

315
00:43:02,622 --> 00:43:05,791
- I'm a little worried about things.
- Oh, really?

316
00:43:05,792 --> 00:43:08,043
I'm worried about how things were handled

317
00:43:08,044 --> 00:43:10,170
without being reported to headquarters.

318
00:43:10,171 --> 00:43:13,673
For instance, the audit team's
investigation of the bus bombing

319
00:43:13,674 --> 00:43:15,510
seems to be quietly fizzling out.

320
00:43:16,427 --> 00:43:19,472
I honestly don't know how long
I can keep covering up around here.

321
00:43:20,431 --> 00:43:22,099
We need to be transparent.

322
00:43:22,100 --> 00:43:26,687
The penalty will be harsh, I'm sure.
It's protocol. I know that it will be.

323
00:43:27,772 --> 00:43:29,398
Who takes the penalty?

324
00:43:34,237 --> 00:43:35,695
I do.

325
00:43:35,696 --> 00:43:38,865
Yeah, well,
you'd probably take the penalty,

326
00:43:38,866 --> 00:43:41,034
which is why I'm calling it
to your attention.

327
00:43:41,035 --> 00:43:44,329
Just do your job and don't worry about it.

328
00:43:44,330 --> 00:43:46,332
I'll take care of everything.

329
00:43:48,584 --> 00:43:49,585
Right.

330
00:43:50,628 --> 00:43:55,340
I hope you'll give it some thought,
even if it's just for ten minutes

331
00:43:55,341 --> 00:43:56,801
while you're in the bathroom.

332
00:44:08,062 --> 00:44:10,731
Dense people have shorter lifespans.

333
00:44:15,319 --> 00:44:19,407
I remember the most interesting thing
I learned in the field.

334
00:44:22,785 --> 00:44:26,538
Sometimes people die
without ever knowing why.

335
00:44:26,539 --> 00:44:28,124
They always have this look.

336
00:44:30,668 --> 00:44:31,794
"Huh?"

337
00:44:32,837 --> 00:44:34,672
They don't understand at all.

338
00:44:38,384 --> 00:44:41,220
I'm pretty sure
that lawyer will have that look.

339
00:44:43,306 --> 00:44:44,307
"Huh?"

340
00:44:47,018 --> 00:44:49,770
Why does that woman always talk like that?

341
00:44:55,234 --> 00:44:57,445
It pisses me off.

342
00:45:23,387 --> 00:45:24,555
Look straight ahead.

343
00:45:31,270 --> 00:45:35,106
It's up to the branch chief
if she wants to report to headquarters.

344
00:45:35,107 --> 00:45:38,611
The legal team shouldn't butt their nose
where it doesn't belong.

345
00:45:40,238 --> 00:45:43,531
Yeah, it's just that I'm trying to do
the job that I was hired to do.

346
00:45:43,532 --> 00:45:44,575
And part of that--

347
00:45:46,494 --> 00:45:47,828
Turn around.

348
00:45:50,915 --> 00:45:52,792
Just do your job properly.

349
00:45:53,834 --> 00:45:56,837
Bus bombing is still being investigated
by the audit team.

350
00:45:58,047 --> 00:45:59,674
Don't cross the line.

351
00:46:02,260 --> 00:46:04,804
- Is that understood?
- Yeah.

352
00:46:17,733 --> 00:46:19,777
Oh, this is fucking ridiculous.

353
00:46:20,778 --> 00:46:24,031
How does everyone keep getting
into my car?

354
00:47:01,610 --> 00:47:03,487
How are you still eating?

355
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:05,614
These snacks are great.

356
00:47:07,867 --> 00:47:09,743
Did you buy those clothes?

357
00:47:09,744 --> 00:47:11,203
They look stupid.

358
00:47:18,377 --> 00:47:20,171
It's good to have you back, chief.

359
00:47:23,174 --> 00:47:25,967
Are you sure
the intel from Babylon is solid?

360
00:47:25,968 --> 00:47:27,678
We're not cops on a stakeout.

361
00:47:28,554 --> 00:47:30,264
How long are we supposed to sit here?

362
00:47:32,558 --> 00:47:33,559
Over there.

363
00:48:02,088 --> 00:48:03,422
Follow my lead.

364
00:48:04,048 --> 00:48:07,175
Capture her alive as quietly as possible.

365
00:48:07,176 --> 00:48:08,177
Copy that.

366
00:48:23,776 --> 00:48:25,319
Light in the face of death…

367
00:49:02,940 --> 00:49:04,483
Jeong Jinman?

368
00:49:09,238 --> 00:49:10,406
Remember, alive!

369
00:49:16,745 --> 00:49:17,788
Q?

370
00:49:26,297 --> 00:49:28,924
- When was this?
- Two hours, give or take.

371
00:49:30,384 --> 00:49:34,345
- You should have reported it immediately.
- My apologies.

372
00:49:34,346 --> 00:49:37,683
It wasn't confirmed information,
so I wanted to check with Intel.

373
00:49:38,267 --> 00:49:41,269
If Q finds out it wasn't Jinman
that killed her younger brother,

374
00:49:41,270 --> 00:49:43,022
I guarantee
that bitch won't just sit there!

375
00:49:48,861 --> 00:49:52,114
Shit! Why is everything
so fucking complicated?

376
00:49:57,119 --> 00:49:59,038
I'm hungry. Let's go eat.

377
00:50:20,184 --> 00:50:21,519
Who's that?

378
00:50:39,245 --> 00:50:41,080
Great. It's the bitch.

379
00:50:51,840 --> 00:50:52,883
What is it?

380
00:50:54,802 --> 00:50:57,513
I haven't heard from you in several days.

381
00:51:55,154 --> 00:51:59,950
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

382
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:09,460
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY KANG JI YOUNG
